{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530745-nexus-crawler-fomori","id":1530745,"title":"Nexus crawler fomori","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-13T08:32:16-08:00","id":1530745,"title":"Nexus crawler fomori","content":"Nexus crawlers are better described as natural disaster especially because of their ability to change reality at will. But waht would happen if the nexus crawler was fused with a human? Or even bsd?<br /> The first answer would be that they would crave to destroy everything and succomb to madness, but would they gain the ability to manipulate reality like the bane do? What would it give to other splat since we know vampires and mage can become fomori?<br /> <br /> Such a dangerous opponent could be a great final ennemy for my story, i would like to make it right so i can make my pc tremble a bit<br /> If you were to create such a monster what ability would you give him if he were<br /> -Human<br /> -Animal<br /> -Vampire (Tremere using a ritual to gain power without truly knowing what he deal with)<br /> -Mage (hoping to get free of paradox)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T14:30:52-08:00","id":1530756,"title":"","content":"For a all of the above:<br /> I would give them the Berserker, Bestial Mutation, Cause Insanity, and Sense Gaia Fomori Powers<br /> <br /> Human:<br /> Give them Immunity to Delirium in addition to the powers above and access to 1 Sphere up to the 3rd level of your choice. Use Willpower instead of Arete<br /> <br /> Animal:<br /> Add Unnatural Strength and the Roar of the Wyrm power, boost animal's intelligence for a dark cunning<br /> <br /> Vampire:<br /> Add the Maw of the Wyrm power, have it work with the kiss Vampires get, gain +2 bonus die to blood magic, increase Generation by 3<br /> <br /> Mage:<br /> Give Eyes of the Wyrm, Reduce paradox by 1 on all casts, Uses Arete or Willpower whichever is higher, gain one sphere in entropy<br /> <br /> Just some ideas off the top of my head","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28181-a-bunch-of-gamers","name":"A Bunch of Gamers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28181_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T15:02:44-08:00","id":1530760,"title":"","content":"The only example we have (Tsannik from Rage) essentially just uses the vessel as a meat suit for acting in the physical realm. Said vessel, a human, has no real autonomy of his own anymore and will die the first time that Tsannik needs to do anything. It basically just has the bane able to use Warp Reality as-is while in the human host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T03:16:59-08:00","id":1530795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Bunch of Gamers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530745-nexus-crawler-fomori?p=1530756#post1530756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a all of the above:<br /> I would give them the Berserker, Bestial Mutation, Cause Insanity, and Sense Gaia Fomori Powers<br /> <br /> Human:<br /> Give them Immunity to Delirium in addition to the powers above and access to 1 Sphere up to the 3rd level of your choice. Use Willpower instead of Arete<br /> <br /> Animal:<br /> Add Unnatural Strength and the Roar of the Wyrm power, boost animal's intelligence for a dark cunning<br /> <br /> Vampire:<br /> Add the Maw of the Wyrm power, have it work with the kiss Vampires get, gain +2 bonus die to blood magic, increase Generation by 3<br /> <br /> Mage:<br /> Give Eyes of the Wyrm, Reduce paradox by 1 on all casts, Uses Arete or Willpower whichever is higher, gain one sphere in entropy<br /> <br /> Just some ideas off the top of my head</div> </div> </div> </div>Thoses are greats, i'll just let them have the bend reality charms except animals who will just create unwilling glitch in reality around them<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The only example we have (Tsannik from Rage) essentially just uses the vessel as a meat suit for acting in the physical realm. Said vessel, a human, has no real autonomy of his own anymore and will die the first time that Tsannik needs to do anything. It basically just has the bane able to use Warp Reality as-is while in the human host.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't know this one but the description i've found on white wolf wiki stick good on the idea i had for my final","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T06:38:44-08:00","id":1530809,"title":"","content":"By the way, just a simple detail i'm not sure how to deal with ben reality charms. If the Nexus Crawler get 5 success the w20 description says it can turn bones into rotten wood and your blood into acid, that kind of thing... does that mean the nexus crawler can instant kill a garou with 5 success?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T08:44:11-08:00","id":1530822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530745-nexus-crawler-fomori?p=1530809#post1530809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, just a simple detail i'm not sure how to deal with ben reality charms. If the Nexus Crawler get 5 success the w20 description says it can turn bones into rotten wood and your blood into acid, that kind of thing... does that mean the nexus crawler can instant kill a garou with 5 success?</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly yes, but recall that if the Garou makes the Rage roll to recover from death, it takes two kills to make it stick (you can only do that once per scene, and the battle scars that result are much more severe).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T03:19:36-08:00","id":1530964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530745-nexus-crawler-fomori?p=1530822#post1530822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possibly yes, but recall that if the Garou makes the Rage roll to recover from death, it takes two kills to make it stick (you can only do that once per scene, and the battle scars that result are much more severe).</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, it's just that if all his bone has turned into rotten wood the healing process will be... well at least awfully painfull considering his body will expell the old bones and regrow new ones. Unless the regeneration cancel the reality modification and turn the wood into bones again but it seems unlikely","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T04:08:49-08:00","id":1530968,"title":"","content":"I'd make them a cult leader. Selling others on aspirations of reality being whatever they say it is. Talking about visions and that the &quot;great one&quot; is coming someday. Basically, use this fomor as a means of creating a slow-burner. This story ends with the group successfully opening a means for the nexus crawler to materialize, with it eventually controlling all of these people. Then you don't have just the nexus crawler, but a legion of fanatical followers to place themselves between the Garou and the nexus crawler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-16T11:57:18-08:00","id":1530996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mundusartis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530745-nexus-crawler-fomori?p=1530968#post1530968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd make them a cult leader. Selling others on aspirations of reality being whatever they say it is. Talking about visions and that the &quot;great one&quot; is coming someday. Basically, use this fomor as a means of creating a slow-burner. This story ends with the group successfully opening a means for the nexus crawler to materialize, with it eventually controlling all of these people. Then you don't have just the nexus crawler, but a legion of fanatical followers to place themselves between the Garou and the nexus crawler.</div> </div> </div> </div>A very good plot indeed, i was going for a fanatic vampire seeking power to ruler over the camarilla and face ante when the gehenna will come, a mad and afraid immortal ready to do everything he can to survive without thinking about what being the host of an entity that powerfull and corrupted imply. I even thougth about made him turn into a living blood creature (pretty much like a symbiote in spider-man comics) looking for more blood, growing and consuming every living being it bond with","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-17T10:44:58-08:00","id":1531027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530745-nexus-crawler-fomori?p=1530964#post1530964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, it's just that if all his bone has turned into rotten wood the healing process will be... well at least awfully painfull considering his body will expell the old bones and regrow new ones. Unless the regeneration cancel the reality modification and turn the wood into bones again but it seems unlikely</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the last ditch Rage recovery roll can also technically allow them to recover from bodily destruction from silver, the crawler's efforts aren't necessarily even the most painful experience that they can recover from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-17T14:59:04-08:00","id":1531035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530745-nexus-crawler-fomori?p=1531027#post1531027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since the last ditch Rage recovery roll can also technically allow them to recover from bodily destruction from silver, the crawler's efforts aren't necessarily even the most painful experience that they can recover from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I put a line for 2 case as ST, i don't care how many limbs, organs has been lost, i don't care what kind of wound caused it, would it be acid, fire, turn into stone... The only case i don't allow the rage recovery is decapitation (mainly because i love Highlander but also because even if the head regrow the character will only be an empty shell of meat without his memory and personality) and the heart complete destruction (because i like the idea of the heart being the source of life from a spiritual point of view).<br /> <br /> Obviously the bigger's the body destruction the worst will be the battle scar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-17T18:02:13-08:00","id":1531045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530745-nexus-crawler-fomori?p=1531035#post1531035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I put a line for 2 case as ST, i don't care how many limbs, organs has been lost, i don't care what kind of wound caused it, would it be acid, fire, turn into stone... The only case i don't allow the rage recovery is decapitation (mainly because i love Highlander but also because even if the head regrow the character will only be an empty shell of meat without his memory and personality) and the heart complete destruction (because i like the idea of the heart being the source of life from a spiritual point of view).<br /> <br /> Obviously the bigger's the body destruction the worst will be the battle scar</div> </div> </div> </div>Who's to say that the body couldn't grow under the old head, or that the spirit couldn't hold some piece of the heart?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T16:36:02-08:00","id":1531075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530745-nexus-crawler-fomori?p=1531045#post1531045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who's to say that the body couldn't grow under the old head, or that the spirit couldn't hold some piece of the heart?</div> </div> </div> </div>Real question or joke x) ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T22:17:15-08:00","id":1531090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530745-nexus-crawler-fomori?p=1531075#post1531075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Real question or joke x) ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do tire of just following Highlander. Also, the existence of the Changers is equal parts spirit and flesh, and they do reinforce one another, so there is that to consider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T10:22:57-08:00","id":1531127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530745-nexus-crawler-fomori?p=1531090#post1531090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do tire of just following Highlander. Also, the existence of the Changers is equal parts spirit and flesh, and they do reinforce one another, so there is that to consider.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, very true","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-22T18:05:58-07:00","id":1534566,"title":"","content":"Re-opening the thread to define the actual limitation of bending reality charms, since i'm about to engage a nexus crawler into my story.<br /> <br /> The w20 give some exemple of transformation it can provide, but what about :<br /> <br /> 1)Giving will to things? (Ex: this fire fly and attack my foe)<br /> <br /> 2)Summoning beings/things ?(a wall of toxic gaz, a monster to defend him...) and how much (summon a storm/tornado....)<br /> <br /> 3)affect mentaly an opponent with something else than illusions? (madness, triggering ptsd, submitting to his will...)<br /> <br /> 4)controlling external energy? (Turning something into gnosis and regain essence, vomitting thunder, increase fire intensity...)<br /> <br /> Adfitionnaly, how as an ST should i decide of the effect? Before the roll and risking failing because of the too little success or after the roll?<br /> <br /> Are the change permanent? If it change my face with 1 success as described in w20 would it go back to normal after sometimes?<br /> <br /> Finally (for now at least) if the effect is directly on a living being, should he be able to resist? Through willpower roll for exemple ? I ask this one because garou and vampire can resist this kind of thing when Mage are using similar tricks (life/spirit sphere to turn garou into chair or something else) and because in w5 it become possible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-22T21:45:55-07:00","id":1534573,"title":"","content":"So first off, keep in mind that Nexus Crawlers aren't rational, at least not in the way we think of them. Nexus Crawler don't take &quot;optimal&quot; actions, and can often take actions that work against itself. It's just that they're so powerful, even if they are doing weird stuff, there's still a high chance that they'll end up killing anything trying to fight them. They can warp reality in almost any way possible, but also in ways that aren't necessarily beneficial.<br /> <br /> So like with 1) yes a Nexus Crawler could turn a fire sentient. But maybe the fire decides that the smartest course of action is get away from the crazy, dangerous, powerful Nexus Crawler. So it spends its turns trying to run away. Maybe it hurts the PCs as it escapes, but it's not going to stick around fighting. In fact, depending on the situation, maybe it could even start attacking the Nexus Crawler if escape isn't possible. <br /> <br /> 2), 3) and 4) are all yes. But again, keep in mind that it won't be acting optimally. Maybe it summons up a bunch of creatures and then the next turn drops a massive fiery explosion on the area, hurting the PCs but also killing most of the things that it just summoned the last turn.<br /> <br /> As for how long changes inflicted by Nexus Crawlers last, I would say against non-supernatural beings the changes are permanent. For supernatural beings (werewolves, mages, etc) I'd roll a die and depending on the result the change is permanent. A roll of 1-9 for vampires and the change is temporary. For werewolves 1-7 and it's temporary. For changelings and wraiths it would be 1-5. And then 1-3 for mages. If temporary, I'd have the change last for at least 24 hours to no more than a week. If the effect is permanent then they'd need to use magic to revert the change. <br /> <br /> For mental attacks I'd allow players to roll or spend Willpower to resist. For physical changes I'd give them a Stamina roll, or let them spend Blood Points or Rage or something like that to shrug off the transformation (or reduce it to only lasting for a couple of turns). <br /> <br /> Ultimately Nexus Crawlers are really powerful, and depending on how things go it's entirely possible to have one TPK your players. But again, they're really chaotic and likely to take actions which undermine their own success chances, and that tends to be what gives a pack of werewolves (or whatever) a chance to defeat one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T02:24:09-07:00","id":1534579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530745-nexus-crawler-fomori?p=1534573#post1534573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So first off, keep in mind that Nexus Crawlers aren't rational, at least not in the way we think of them. Nexus Crawler don't take &quot;optimal&quot; actions, and can often take actions that work against itself. It's just that they're so powerful, even if they are doing weird stuff, there's still a high chance that they'll end up killing anything trying to fight them. They can warp reality in almost any way possible, but also in ways that aren't necessarily beneficial.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was aware of this part but it's always a good thing to remind, even the books tell Nexus Crawler are more like natural disaster than actual predator.<br /> Now that you confirm that all this are possible when nexus crawler are unleashed it's understandable why they're so scary, when you face one you never know what will happen and it can be anything","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T07:08:01-07:00","id":1534586,"title":"","content":"Can Nexus Crawler affect time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T10:16:18-07:00","id":1534598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530745-nexus-crawler-fomori?p=1534586#post1534586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Nexus Crawler affect time?</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be a bit of a reserved capability that you don't find very often in W:tA. In any case, if you want it to, you'll probably want to pick up Shattered Dreams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T10:37:22-07:00","id":1534599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530745-nexus-crawler-fomori?p=1534586#post1534586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Nexus Crawler affect time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Logically i would say yes but not with time travelling or stopping, more like slow down your mental capacity/movement or alike.<br /> <br /> I think there's a greater chance for nexus crawler to destroy and change physical thing and physical laws (gravity, speed...) rather than time and space","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-22T12:07:32-07:00","id":1536106,"title":"","content":"There is no reason for a Nexus Crawler to not be able to change time and space, or to do any other thing.<br /> <br /> What's the question is if as the ST you should. Since it isn't a rational agent, ultimately the creature only does whatever the ST wants it to do, and you shouldn't complain about the result to your chronicle afterwards, you'll be the only one to blame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}